  "context": "During the chdb-4x tuning follow-up (merged as PR #2719), the 4.x engine could not be loaded locally (dyld mis-aligned LINKEDIT; long venv paths truncated the diagnosis), so whether 4.x resolves the 3.6.0 timestamp/hang reports was never directly verified. The merge-time conclusion rests on inference, not on loading the engine.\n\n2026-11-07: the locked chDB 4.1.6 wheel still does not load on macOS arm64 (seen during #4012). Arrow parity ran on 3.7.2 instead; see chdb-rows-nan-vs-arrow-null-q17-20261107.\n\n2026-11-07 delivered in PR #4036 (merge commit 1c1651e7a66131d768ac1c8c9de10b2920bd6f0d). macOS arm64: chdb 4.1.6 (short path /tmp/c4) still fails to import: dlopen mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool. Linux aarch64 (Apple container 1.1.0, python:3.12-slim, uv sync --frozen: chdb 4.1.6, chdb-core 26.1.0): engine loads; TIMESTAMP NOT NULL metadata column round-trips exactly (DateTime, 2026-11-07 12:34:56); tuning metadata create/marker/save/load path completes in 1.2 s with no hang; 10 real-CLI clickhouse-local tuning-liveness cells pass in 76.6 s (/tmp/rv/chdb4x-run2.log). Conclusion: the 3.6.0 timestamp/hang behavior is not reproduced on 4.1.6; confirmed fixed on Linux. Durable guard: tests/integration/platforms/test_chdb_engine_load.py and scripts/verify_chdb_engine.py run in the Linux medium CI job (passed in PR CI) and fail there instead of skipping; macOS skips only on the LINKEDIT load failure. Caveat: the original 3.6.0 error text was not found in the repo/tracker, so the behavior class was verified rather than the exact string; 3.6.0 was not re-run.",
